---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why Systems Field Guide explains engineering choices through constraints and trade-offs."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <p class="hero-kicker">About</p><h1>
        A guide for making contextual choices.
      </h1><p>
        Systems Field Guide is a growing collection of practical explanations
        for developers learning how architecture decisions behave outside a
        feature checklist.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner article-content">
      <h2>What this collection values</h2>
      <p>
        Technology choices are rarely contests with a permanent winner. Workload
        shape, consistency requirements, team experience, operational capacity,
        time horizon, and failure tolerance all change the answer. Each concept
        therefore starts with a mental model and makes its constraints visible.
      </p>
      <p>
        The diagrams and comparisons aim to be useful at a whiteboard, during
        design review, or while learning an unfamiliar part of the stack.
        Official documentation remains the source for detailed product behavior;
        this guide focuses on the reasoning that connects behavior to choices.
      </p>
      <h2>Who makes it</h2>
      <p>
        The guide is written and maintained by <a
          href="https://github.com/Oscar-Espinoza"
          rel="me">Oscar Espinoza</a
        >. It is intentionally quiet about authorship on the homepage so the
        material, not a résumé, stays central.
      </p>
      <h2>Publishing approach</h2>
      <p>
        Entries may be marked <em>evolving</em> when the core explanation is useful
        but the guide is still expanding. Dates and official references make review
        easier. Drafts are never included in production routes, search, sitemaps,
        or related links.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
